# ORPHANED (no longer in localnetworks_en.lex; kept for reference, commented out by lex-to-po.pl): 'ln_Local networks' => 'Sieci lokalne',
'ln_FIRSTPAGE_DESC' => ' For security reasons, several services on your server are available only to your local network. However you can grant these local access privileges to additional networks by listing them below. Most installations should leave this list empty. Add network ',
'ln_ADD_TITLE' => 'Dodaj sieć lokalną',
'ln_ADD_DESC' => '(en)Each parameter must be in the form #.#.#.# (each # is a number from 0 to 255). The server software will zero out the ending (host identifier) part of the network address according to the subnet mask, to ensure that the network address is valid.  "Router" should be the IP address of the router on your local network via which the additional network is reached.',
